  "Id": 918,
  "Title": "AKUH successfully treats first bone marrow transplant patient",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "The first patient treated at the new Bone Marrow Transplant (BMT) Unit at Aga Khan University Hospital (AKUH) was recently discharged from the Hospital after successful treatment lasting 26 days.",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The first patient treated at the new Bone Marrow Transplant (BMT) Unit at Aga Khan University Hospital (AKUH) was recently discharged from the Hospital after successful treatment lasting 26 days."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Amir Wahid Mughal, 28, from Gujranwala had been diagnosed with Hodgkin's disease six months after his marriage and was undergoing initial treatment at a hospital in Lahore. He approached the BMT Unit after seeing an announcement in a newspaper, and a diagnostic test qualified him to undergo Autologous Bone Marrow Transplantation at AKUH. Describing the transplantation as a success for the entire BMT team, Dr Irfan Vaziri, Assistant Professor and Consultant Haematologist and Oncologist, and Dr Salman Adil Assistant Professor and Consultant Haematologistcommended the professionalism of BMT trained nurses as well as AKUH's state-of-the-art Laboratory and Blood Bank Services."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Inaugurated in April 2004, the BMT Unit at AKUH is specially designed for a select group of oncology and haematology patients, offering services to patients suffering from benign and malignant disorders such as aplastic anaemia, lymphoma, leukaemia and thalassaemia. AKUH is one of the few teaching hospitals in the world to be ISO 9001 certified, combining high-quality clinical service with compassionate, ethical, accessible and individualistic patient care that meets the needs and expectations of its patients."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "\"This is just the first step. Amir has returned to Gujranwala and is living a normal life with his family. He is still in contact with usand adhering to a follow-up regimen at AKUH\", said Dr. Vaziri."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
